# The three `-ov` command types (for the predictive-syntax dropdown)

Machine-readable copy: [ov_command_types.json](ov_command_types.json). Every example below was run against current data.
All three types are the same idea: **`nspe <sport> <player> [-<stat>N] -ov [filter] [window]`** -- short, readable, and the
same in NFL, MLB, NBA and NHL.

## 1. Overview -- "everything about him"
`nspe <sport> <player> -ov [window]`   window: season (default) | `YYYY` | `YYYY-YYYY` | `-career` | `-lastN`

| Sport | Command | Shows |
|---|---|---|
| NFL | `nspe nfl mahomes -ov -career` | yards by quarter and half (Q1-Q4, 1H, 2H, FULL) |
| MLB | `nspe mlb judge -ov 2025` | batting line split home / away / total |
| NBA | `nspe nba curry -ov -career` | one row per season + totals, per-game lines, record |
| NHL | `nspe nhl mcdavid -ov` | goals, assists, points, +/-, shots this season |

## 2. Count line -- "how many games did he clear a number?"
`nspe <sport> <player> -<stat>N -ov [window]`   (N = the threshold; N-or-more games)

| Sport | Command | Shows |
|---|---|---|
| NFL | `nspe nfl mahomes -yds300 -ov -career` | 51/128 games, with dates |
| NFL | `nspe nfl jamarr -rcpt10 -ov -career` | 10+ reception games |
| MLB | `nspe mlb yordan -dub1 -ov 2020-2026` | 159/790 games (total 173 doubles, last match 2026-09-23 @ SEA) |
| MLB | `nspe mlb judge -hr1 -ov -career` | home-run games (`-hits`/`-hr`/`-tb` also show batting AVG) |
| NBA | `nspe nba curry -pts30 -ov -career` | 30+ point games |
| NBA | `nspe nba durant -tpm4 -ov 2020-2026` | 4+ threes since 2020 |
| NHL | `nspe nhl mcdavid -pts2 -ov` | multi-point games this season |

Terminal: one count line (NFL also lists the games). Every game is always in the JSON `results` (newest first).

## 3. Narrowed count -- "the same count, but only ..."
`nspe <sport> <player> -<stat>N -ov <filter> [window]`

| Filter | Command | Shows |
|---|---|---|
| `vs <team>` | `nspe nfl jamarr -rcpt10 vs pit -career` | 3/8 games against the Steelers |
| `vs <team>` | `nspe mlb judge -hr1 vs bos -career` | home-run games against the Red Sox |
| `vs <team>` | `nspe nhl mcdavid -pts2 -ov vs cgy -career` | multi-point games against the Flames |
| half / quarter | `nspe nfl dak 1h -yds150 -ov -career` | 150+ first-half passing yards |
| playoff round | `nspe nfl mahomes -yds250 -sb -ov` | 250+ yards in Super Bowls (`-wild -div -champ -sb`) |
| last N | `nspe nfl mahomes -yds300 -ov -last10` | 300+ yards in his last 10 games |
| last N | `nspe nba curry -pts30 -ov -last20` | 30+ points in his last 20 games |

Notes: `vs <team>` defaults to career; `-lastN` with `vs` = the latest N meetings; 0/8 is a valid answer. NBA `vs <team>` is
waiting on an opponent column in the scrape; MLB/NBA/NHL playoff-round flags are waiting on round labels; NFL also has
`mnf`/`snf`/`tnf` and quarter scopes `q1`-`q4`.

## Stat tokens by sport (the `<stat>` in `-<stat>N`)
- **NFL:** `-yds` `-td` `-rcpt` `-tgt`   (category words `pass` / `rush` / `rec` pick which; `-td` counts that category's TDs)
- **MLB:** `-hr` `-hits` `-rbi` `-runs` `-bb` `-sb` `-2b`/`-dub` `-3b` `-tb` `-total` `-hrr`
- **NBA:** `-pts` `-reb` `-ast` `-stl` `-blk` `-tpm` `-min`
- **NHL:** `-g` `-a` `-pts` `-sog` `-ppg` `-ppa` `-ppp` `-gwg` `-pm`

## Tips for the dropdown
- The player name is the only free-text part; everything else is a fixed vocabulary, so it completes well as the user types.
- Suggest Type 2 first for a stat-minded user (`-pts30 -ov`), Type 1 when only a name has been typed.
- Every command also works in plain English (`how many 10 reception games does chase have vs the steelers` maps to the syntax above).
